 "key_insight": "The Royal Kennel Club ranks on registry authority and does have a Staffordshire Bull Terrier breed page, but that page is a registry profile (traits, standard colours, recommended health tests, registration rules) that hands the buyer to a generic all-breed puppy search. BSUK can beat it for the buyer by pairing the same health-test list (HC-HSF4, L-2-HGA, elbow and eye schemes) with its own dogs' results, visible litters and a Staffy-specific buyer checklist on one open page."
